.SH description
.B venti
is a linux-only terminal multiplexer. client/server over local unix domain sockets.

starts daemon, manages sessions, panes, ptys. detach cleanly. reattach later.

dwindle tiling (binary splits, aspect-aware). workspaces. floating windows.
layout persists on restart.

mouse: click, drag, wheel. f-keys everywhere.

terminal graphics (sixel, kitty, iterm2) are experimental and may be
unreliable across terminal emulators, particularly on resize, scroll and
layout changes. graphics is on by default; set graphics = false in
~/.config/venti/config.toml if images glitch, or turn it off from f2 -> graphics.
venti doctor prints the same reminder.

.SH commands
.TP
.B venti
attach default session

.TP
.B venti run -t default workspace_goto 2
switch to workspace 2 via command line

.TP
.B venti run -t default close_workspace 2 3
close workspaces 2 and 3

.TP
.B venti run -t default move_to_workspace 4
move focused pane to workspace 4


.TP
.B venti new \-s \fIname\fR
create and attach named session

.TP
.B venti attach \-t \fIname\fR
attach to session

.TP
.B venti attach \-d \-t \fIname\fR
attach, kick off other clients

.TP
.B venti ls
list sessions

.TP
.B venti kill \-t \fIname\fR
terminate session

.TP
.B venti send \-t \fIname\fR \fIkeys\fR
send keys to pane

.TP
.B venti paste \-t \fIname\fR
paste clipboard to pane (or stdin with \fB\-\-stdin\fR)

.TP
.B venti config init
create config at ~/.config/venti/config.toml

.TP
.B venti config check
validate config

.TP
.B venti config path
show config path

.TP
.B venti doctor
check terminal capabilities

.TP
.B venti completions \fIshell\fR
generate completions (bash|fish|zsh|elvish)

.TP
.B venti kill-server
stop the background daemon; kills every session and removes stale sockets

.TP
.B venti man
print the manual page (this page)

